".i ta ri'u ve'i finpe" is a sentence used in the reference grammar to show
the usage of one of the VEhA series.
As I understand it, (ve'i) is a word indicating that the object/event
occupies a small area of space.
If this is true, would it describe it's referent as small (where 'small' is
relevant to context)?

